tment in social rent  would enable large construction sites to  keep going it would enable  us as a sector to withstand the risk of  a turbulent market cycle so  as bob said also um we had a real  reduction in funding for social housing  from 2010 onwards we have have some  funding now but we've been much more  um we've been building homes for sale as  well as the sector to cross subsidize  our affordable programs  and that becomes impossible in the  downturn there isn't that cross subsidy  so  our one ask would be yeah investment in  social rent  from grant and john  sketch out to me here the kind of  planning system that you  envisage well is it a kind of zonal  system  where uh as in the white paper where in  certain places you know  any development that that is in in line  with the the aesthetic of the area  um would get automatic permission to be  built is that what is that what kind of  system you think you need  to solve a problem so there's no doubt  having more certainty in the system what  everyone can know what's going to happen  and what's allowed would be better  but a zonal system doesn't necessarily  get you all the way so you still have  the question of  what you're going to zone and where 40  of the buildings in manhattan you  couldn't build today because the current  zoning will prohibit it  so you've still got this question of  what you're going to allow  for me um you you published a piece on  the spectator website a month ago it  should have outlined this idea of if you  gave  local control to residents on very small  scales a single street  or a single block and they can work out  for themselves what designs are  acceptable what they can all live with  and they can allow gradual addition of  density over time  that's a much more sustainable way of  supplementing what's coming through in  the existing system in a way that local  people are actually happy with  and you can add enormous volumes of  housing that way where it's most needed  brilliant well all that is now left me  to do is to thank uh our speakers today  uh to thank bob uh kate and john it's  been an  absolutely fascinating discussion and to  thank you all for your questions it's um  slightly odd not to be able to look at  you to say thank you but  thank you anyway um there are plenty  more events  to come in the spectators alternative  conference so this lunch time we're  having a live recording of  coffeehouse shots and this afternoon  we're having an event on  uh the best way to get to net zero so  hope to see you  back for some more of those events but  um uh i would normally say if you give  our speakers a round of applause but um  i i i i shan't uh seeing as  uh not sure david hee but um just  express your thanks to our speakers  and thank you all so much for tuning in  good night
 

